        "Memory Subsystems & Chiplets",
        "Semiconductor Engineering"
      ],
      "text": "Fil-C retrofits spatial and temporal memory safety onto C and C++ programs using software capabilities (InvisiCaps) checked on every pointer dereference. However, Fil-C relies on an unstated hardware assumption that DRAM reliably preserves capability metadata. In Fil-C, each heap pointer's upper-bound word is stored inline in ordinary DRAM without hardware integrity protection.",
      "token_count": 52
    },
