      "text": "A single 0-to-1 bit-flip induced by Rowhammer in a pointer's upper-bound metadata expands the pointer's permitted memory range by 2^k bytes. Because the runtime treats the corrupted upper bound as authoritative, it silently permits out-of-bounds reads and writes without raising any panic, signal, or exception.",
